  <div id="sutta">
  
                <h3 id="AN6.83" class="h1">The Foremost State<br/>
                  Aggadhamma Sutta  (AN 6:83)</h3><!--end suttahead-->
<p>“Monks, endowed with six qualities, a monk is incapable of attaining arahantship, the foremost state. Which six?</p>
<p>“There is the case where a monk is without conviction, is shameless, is without compunction, is lazy, is undiscerning, and is concerned with his body &amp; life.</p>
<p>“Endowed with these six qualities, a monk is incapable of attaining arahantship, the foremost state.</p>
<p>“Monks, endowed with six qualities, a monk is capable of attaining arahantship, the foremost state. Which six?</p>
<p>“There is the case where a monk has conviction, has a sense of shame, has compunction, has his persistence aroused, is discerning, and is unconcerned with his body &amp; life.</p>
<p>“Endowed with these six qualities, a monk is capable of attaining arahantship, the foremost state.”</p>
<p class="seealso">See also: <a href="AN5_2.html" class="sutta-ref">AN 5:2</a>; <a href="../KN/StNp/StNp2_10.html" class="sutta-ref">Sn 2:10</a>; <a href="../KN/StNp/StNp3_2.html" class="sutta-ref">Sn 3:2</a>; <a href="../KN/Thag/thag2_37.html" class="sutta-ref">Thag 2:37</a></p>


      </div><!--end:sutta-->
